<Slide style={{ width: 1280, height: 720, background: '#0A1020', fontFamily: 'Arial', padding: '52px 60px 30px 60px', display: 'flex', flexDirection: 'column' }}>
    <Text style={{ fontSize: 12, color: '#4D8DFF', fontWeight: 'bold', letterSpacing: 2.2 }}>08 · CONCLUSIONS</Text>
    <Text style={{ fontSize: 32, fontWeight: 'bold', color: '#FFFFFF', lineHeight: 1.2, marginTop: 8 }}>
        Four claims we can defend — with their strength attached
    </Text>
    <Box style={{ width: 1160, height: 1, background: '#24334C', marginTop: 14 }} />

    <Box style={{ flexDirection: 'column', marginTop: 10 }}>
        {[
            ['01', 'Chain information mostly does not pay', '12 of 19 cells sit below zero, median −0.098. The most stable negative is on the data-richest task: op_tm × A3 = −0.859 over 75 computable rows.'],
            ['02', 'Stratification is refuted, but not cleanly tested', 'ρ = +0.000 / +0.239. At matched n, tier 1 stays below tier 2 (−0.033 / −0.087, intervals excluding zero) — so the break is inside tier 3, not the sample-size confound.'],
            ['03', 'More data does not buy it back', 'κ = −0.0863 [−0.1053, −0.0672] with Λ ratio 0.650. Under the absolute ruler the same curve halves (0.167) — reported beside H2, never merged into it.'],
            ['04', 'Information versus architecture stays unanswerable', 'A5 cannot be constructed from the data, so its zero count is a boundary, not a debt. The substitute is a per-task floor: median 0.0022, cleared by 6 of 8 tasks.'],
        ].map(([num, head, body], i) => (
            <Box key={num} style={{ flexDirection: 'row', gap: 26, paddingTop: 12, paddingBottom: 12, borderTop: i === 0 ? '0px solid #1D2A40' : '1px solid #1D2A40' }}>
                <Text style={{ fontSize: 22, fontWeight: 'bold', color: '#4D8DFF', width: 46, lineHeight: 1.2 }}>{num}</Text>
                <Box style={{ flexDirection: 'column', flex: 1 }}>
                    <Text style={{ fontSize: 18, fontWeight: 'bold', color: '#FFFFFF', lineHeight: 1.3 }}>{head}</Text>
                    <Text style={{ fontSize: 13, color: '#A8B8CE', marginTop: 5, lineHeight: 1.55 }}>{body}</Text>
                </Box>
            </Box>
        ))}
    </Box>

    <Box style={{ marginTop: 'auto', padding: '10px 18px', background: '#16233A', borderLeft: '2px solid #4D8DFF' }}>
        <Text style={{ fontSize: 14, color: '#FFFFFF', lineHeight: 1.55 }}>
            Within the range we measured, the chain is not what the repeat-unit representation is missing — and the weight of that
            sentence is bounded by two undecidable points and one arm that cannot exist.
        </Text>
    </Box>

    <Box style={{ flexDirection: 'row', justifyContent: 'space-between', marginTop: 12 }}>
        <Text style={{ fontSize: 12, color: '#5E7590' }}>Group 32 · How Much Is a Chain Worth?</Text>
        <Text style={{ fontSize: 12, color: '#5E7590' }}>14 / 17</Text>
    </Box>
</Slide>
